==============================================================================
C7. Power — what this null does and does not rule out
==============================================================================
  The controlled estimate is 1.266, 95% CI 0.856 to 1.872.
  So the data are consistent with anything from a small REDUCTION in
  promotions after the line to a 1.87-fold rise. This is a null with a
  wide interval, not a demonstration that the line does nothing.

  What it does exclude: the doubling-or-more that a widespread, uniform
  practice would leave in a cohort of this size. What it cannot exclude:
  a practice confined to a handful of men a year, which is what the
  well-known individual cases actually look like. 834 first-time roster
  additions fall in the first 45 days of a season across sixteen seasons —
  about 52 a season, of whom the pedigree cut keeps about 8.

